WEBVTT

00:00:30.352 --> 00:00:31.034
<v><b>J:</b></v> Another hour!

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:34.663
<v><b>A:</b></v> Are you also on the London flight?

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.400
<v><b>J:</b></v> Yes, unfortunately.

00:00:37.445 --> 00:00:38.290
Another delay.

00:00:38.932 --> 00:00:40.108
Who knows when we’ll take off…

00:00:41.815 --> 00:00:43.480
<v><b>A:</b></v> Is there someone waiting for you at the airport?

00:00:44.066 --> 00:00:46.978
<v><b>J:</b></v> No… that’s probably a good thing

00:00:48.911 --> 00:00:49.643
<v><b>A:</b></v> No, me neither.

00:00:51.332 --> 00:00:52.261
I’m Alex, by the way.

00:00:54.342 --> 00:00:56.999
You’re British, right? Do you live in London?

00:00:58.043 --> 00:00:58.950
<v><b>J:</b></v> I’m Jake.

00:00:59.056 --> 00:01:01.585
No, I don’t live in the UK, I live in Chicago now.

00:01:02.259 --> 00:01:04.101
I work at Chicago State University.

00:01:04.525 --> 00:01:05.132
<v><b>A:</b></v> Oh, cool.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.243
So why are you going to London?

00:01:07.785 --> 00:01:11.814
<v><b>J:</b></v> I’m going to give a talk at a conference in Oxford, actually.

00:01:14.412 --> 00:01:16.006
<v><b>A:</b></v> So do you like living in Chicago?

00:01:16.249 --> 00:01:17.479
<v><b>J:</b></v> Oh, I love it.

00:01:18.224 --> 00:01:22.669
I’m going to stay there for at least another two years – they’ve extended my contract.

00:01:24.186 --> 00:01:26.365
<v><b>A:</b></v> Yeah, Chicago’s a great city.

00:01:27.743 --> 00:01:30.384
I’m not working, I’m on holiday.

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:33.138
I’m going to do a tour of the UK.

00:01:33.812 --> 00:01:35.031
And I’m going to visit Oxford!

00:01:35.618 --> 00:01:36.100
<v><b>J:</b></v> Oh right.

00:01:36.101 --> 00:01:37.983
That’s er, that’s nice.

00:01:38.896 --> 00:01:39.659
<v><b>A:</b></v> I’m really excited.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.417
It’s my first trip to England.

00:01:41.518 --> 00:01:43.984
<v><b>J:</b></v> Well, I’m sure you’re going to have a great time.

00:01:44.473 --> 00:01:46.514
May’s a great month to be in the UK.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:47.584
<v><b>A:</b></v> I hope so.

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:54.686
Hey, maybe you could show me around Oxford University? Are you going to be there all week?

00:01:55.082 --> 00:02:01.010
<v><b>J:</b></v> Oh, well… I’m going to be very busy, but maybe…

00:02:02.235 --> 00:02:04.038
<v><b>A:</b></v> So your trip is all work, no fun?

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:09.845
<v><b>J:</b></v> Yes – though, well, I’m going to meet up with a friend, well,

00:02:11.243 --> 00:02:14.524
my ex-girlfriend really, who I was with when I was a student.

00:02:14.939 --> 00:02:16.093
She lives in Oxford now.

00:02:16.864 --> 00:02:17.568
<v><b>A:</b></v> That’s great!

00:02:18.176 --> 00:02:23.918
<v><b>J:</b></v> Yeah, we broke up when I got the job in Chicago, but, well…

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:27.486
I’m really looking forward to seeing her.

00:02:30.228 --> 00:02:33.395
<v><b>A:</b></v> Hey, we’re probably not going to leave for some time.

00:02:34.356 --> 00:02:35.415
Let’s have a drink somewhere.

00:02:36.249 --> 00:02:42.000
<v><b>J:</b></v> Um, OK, yes, why not?

00:02:43.452 --> 00:02:45.127
Let’s check the Departures screen first.

00:02:45.405 --> 00:02:47.943
<v><b>A:</b></v> Oh – Jake – is this yours?

00:02:50.481 --> 00:02:52.711
<v><b>J:</b></v> My phone! Thanks.

00:02:52.712 --> 00:02:56.691
Typical me, I always lose things when I’m travelling.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.703
<v><b>A:</b></v> So, text me your number, now, so you don’t forget…